    "probe_text": "Here's the complete ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, read from `owners.POST.yml` and each function class. Every step from `validate` onward runs under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so all DB work commits once at the end.\n\n## Gate (before the pipeline)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Without that role the request is denied (403) before any step runs.\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n**1. `checkIdempotency` (`CheckIdempotencyKey`)** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key has already produced an owner, throws `IdempotentReplayException`, short-circuiting the whole pipeline to return the original owner with **200** (no duplicate created). Otherwise publishes the key (blank = \"no key\") for step 19. *No governance \u2014 does no DB work.*\n\n**2. `validate` (`ValidateOwnerFields`)** \u2014 binds the body (no `@Valid`) and, in this order:\n- *Side-effect:* normalizes the **address** \u2014 prefers structured `addressLine1/2` (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand abbreviations, compose into flat `address`); else normalizes the flat `address` and clears the structured lines.\n- *Validation:* rejects blank (null/whitespace) `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`.\n- *Side-effect + validation:* normalizes **telephone** to E.164 (strips separators, defaults to `+61`, drops a leading national `0`, enforces 8\u201315 digits and fixed national lengths for `+61`=9 / `+1`=10); an unconvertible value is a `telephone` error.\n- *Validation:* runs the bean `Validator` for the remaining schema constraints (`@Email`, `@Pattern`, `@Size`/max-length, etc.).\n- *Validation:* **postcode** \u2014 when present and well-formed, must be in range for the region derived from the city (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown city accepts any 4-digit).\n- Any accumulated errors \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**).\n- *Side-effect:* normalizes **email** to lower case, then publishes the validated body.\n\n**3. `rejectDisposableEmailDomain` (`RejectDisposableEmailDomain`)** \u2014 *Validation:* if the email's domain is on the disposable blocklist \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (**400**).\n\n**4. `rejectFutureRegistrationDate` (`RejectFutureRegistrationDate`)** \u2014 *Validation:* if supplied `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**).\n\n**5. `resolveRegistrationDate` (`ResolveRegistrationDate`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* computes the effective date (supplied or today), rolls weekends/holidays forward to the next business day, and publishes it as a `LocalDate` used by steps 8, 9, 15.\n\n**6. `rejectDuplicateIdentity` (`RejectDuplicateIdentity`)** \u2014 *Validation:* builds an identity key `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone | lowerEmail | soundex(lastName))` and scans all **non-deleted** owners; a match \u2192 `DuplicateIdentityException` (**409**).\n\n**7. `rejectCityAtCapacity` (`RejectCityAtCapacity`)** \u2014 *Validation:* if the city (case-insensitive) already holds \u2265 50 owners \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**).\n\n**8. `rejectDailyLimit` (`RejectDailyOwnerLimit`)** \u2014 *Validation:* if \u2265 100 owners already carry this adjusted business-day `registrationDate` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitException` (**429**).\n\n**9. `build` (`BuildOwner`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* maps the DTO to a new `Owner` entity and stamps the resolved business-day `registrationDate` onto it (overriding any supplied value).\n\n**10. `assignMemberId` (`AssignMemberId`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* computes `memberId` (`<REGION><FY><HASH8><Luhn>`) and appends `-<n>` to de-duplicate against existing member ids.\n\n**11. `assignHousehold` (`AssignHousehold`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* stamps a deterministic `householdId` derived from last name + postcode (unconditional, even for a lone owner).\n\n**12. `assignHouseholdSize` (`AssignHouseholdSize`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* sets `householdMemberCount` = existing members sharing the `householdId` + 1 (this owner).\n\n**13. `countNamesakes` (`AssignNamesakeCount`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**14. `assignMembershipLevel` (`AssignMembershipLevel`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* sets `membershipLevel` = the owner's natural (points-based) level, capped at one above the max level among existing household members (no cap if none).\n\n**15. `flagBulkSignup` (`AssignBulkSignupWarning`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* sets `bulkSignupWarning` true when > 80 owners already share this business day.\n\n**16. `flagCapacityWarning` (`AssignCapacityWarning`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* sets `capacityWarning` true when the city holds 40\u201349 owners (the band just below the hard limit).\n\n**17. `flagPossibleDuplicate` (`AssignPossibleDuplicate`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* unless `sharesHousehold` is declared true, sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` when a non-deleted owner shares the last-name Soundex and postcode but has a different identity key (lowest matching id).\n\n**18. `save` (`SaveOwner`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its generated id).\n\n**19. `recordIdempotency` (`RecordIdempotencyKey`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* if a non-blank `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner id` in the `IdempotencyStore`.\n\n**20. `audit` (`AuditOwnerCreated`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* writes to the `AUDIT` logger \u2014 a human-readable line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel) and a structured `OwnerCreatedEvent` JSON with a process-wide incrementing `seq`.\n\n**21. `enqueueWelcome` (`EnqueueWelcomeNotification`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* writes a welcome line to the `NOTIFY` logger (owner id + memberId).\n\n**22. `respond` (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`)** \u2014 *Side-effect:* maps the owner to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Validation ordering is deliberate:** idempotency replay \u2192 field/format validation \u2192 email/date/identity/capacity/rate rejects \u2192 then all the enrichment/side-effect stamping \u2192 persist \u2192 record/audit/notify \u2192 respond.\n- Because everything from step 2 shares one transaction, any escalation thrown mid-pipeline (400/409/429) rolls back \u2014 no partial owner, no idempotency record, no audit/notify for a rejected create."
